## Macro: `xt/visual/macros/percent_not_on_bracket`

**%** finds the matching bracket only when the cursor is on a bracket character (`()[]{}`). When the cursor is not on a bracket, **%** does nothing.

**Keys:** `%`

**initial.png**
- Cursor at line 1, col 0 (on 'n' of "no brackets here")
- Text contains no bracket characters

**after_percent.png**
- Cursor still at line 1, col 0
- No movement — not on a bracket character
- Buffer unchanged
END_DESC
    run => sub {
        my ($ctx) = @_;
        $ctx->buffer->set_text($CODE);
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('initial');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('%');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_percent');
    },
}__DATA__
